  "verses": {
    "verse": [
      [
        "My grandfather's clock was too large for the shelf,",
        "so it stood ninety years on the floor;",
        "it was taller by half than the old man himself,",
        "though it weighed not a pennyweight more.",
        "It was bought on the morn of the day that he was born,",
        "and was always his treasure and pride;",
        "but it stopp'd short — never to go again —",
        "when the old man died."
      ],
      [
        "In watching its pendulum swing to and fro,",
        "many hours had he spent while a boy;",
        "and in childhood and manhood the clock seemed to know",
        "and to share both his grief and his joy.",
        "For it struck twenty-four when he entered at the door,",
        "with a blooming and beautiful bride;",
        "but it stopp'd short — never to go again —",
        "when the old man died."
      ],
      [
        "My grandfather said that of those he could hire,",
        "not a servant so faithful he found;",
        "for it wasted no time, and had but one desire —",
        "at the close of each week to be wound.",
        "And it kept in its place — not a frown upon its face,",
        "and its hands never hung by its side;",
        "but it stopp'd short — never to go again —",
        "when the old man died."
      ],
      [
        "It rang an alarm in the dead of the night —",
        "an alarm that for years had been dumb;",
        "and we knew that his spirit was pluming for flight —",
        "that his hour of departure had come.",
        "Still the clock kept the time, with a soft and muffled chime,",
        "as we silently stood by his side;",
        "but it stopp'd short — never to go again —",
        "when the old man died."
      ]
    ]
  },
  "arrangerNotes": "Verse 1 and chorus, vocal (soprano) line, verified against the LilyPond score on English Wikipedia; the piano introduction is left out, the verse repeat with first and second endings and the repeated chorus phrase are written out, and the score's 'stopp'd short' rests are kept. No simplification needed. D drum: as written (range low 3 to 5; the 'tick, tick' figure uses the low 3), D minLayout 15. C drum: the C drum has no low 3, so each 'tick, tick, tick, tick' group (score events 91–94 and 102–105) is played one octave higher; C minLayout 11. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum). Lyrics of the added verses: Verses 2–4: Henry Clay Work (1876), as given on English Wikipedia (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Grandfather%27s_Clock). The chorus is sung after every verse.",
  "verified": true
}
